  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Unlocking Accountability and Transparency in public service provision</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project&#x2019;s goal is to establish a robust accountability model that ensures transparency and accountability, fairness, and efficiency in resource distribution and service provision to enhance integrity and community trust.  Chikomba district has 30 wards, but we shall focus only on 10 wards where there are more households that are food insecure. The selection of the wards is based on statistics of the recent vulnerability assessments done in the district.  We plan to engage with duty bearers and raise awareness of their responsibilities but also to equip them with the skills and tools to achieve them.  The duty bearers include traditional leaders, councillors, and others like religious leaders.  We will also engage with other stakeholders responsible and mandated with resource distribution like the Ministry of Public Service, Labour and Social Welfare, and other key stakeholders like Chikomba Rural District Council, DDC, other line ministries and the Chiefs Council.</narrative>
  </description>
